1
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,880
The future content creator.

2
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,000
This time,

3
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,440
I'm not backing down.

4
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:44,800
We have a problem!

5
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,800
We need a new assistant by today.

6
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:48,160
Ms. Alice,

7
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,680
do you still want to work here?

8
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:50,960
I've found someone.

9
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:53,160
I hope she's not useless.

10
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,120
Do you know who I am?

11
00:01:54,479 --> 00:01:55,280
Yes, I do.

12
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:56,440
And from somewhere else?

13
00:01:58,039 --> 00:01:59,680
Isn't that Nannalin?

14
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,240
Her zipper's open.

15
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,600
Should I tell her?

16
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:04,000
Next time,

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,480
if you want to help me,

18
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,400
ask me first.

19
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:07,840
Understood.

20
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,000
Alice.

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,400
The perfume brand urgently needs slide five revised.

22
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,920
Has the boss checked it yet?

23
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,280
I'm counting on you.

24
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,400
Alice!

25
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,440
That influencer with 200,000 subscribers

26
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,079
is asking for another two hours.

27
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,760
Can you get Ms. Nannalin's approval?

28
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:35,960
Please? Pretty please?

29
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:36,760
I'm counting on you.

30
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:37,720
Thank you!

31
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:43,400
Yesterday's conversion summary is on this desk.

32
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,840
Please have the boss sign it.

33
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,680
Hey, wait...

34
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,200
Slide five! Five!

35
00:02:54,079 --> 00:02:56,040
These are all the previous campaign records

36
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,480
you need to read

37
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:58,560
and understand.

38
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,240
All of these?

39
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:03,920
Yes.

40
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,160
Every single one.

41
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,280
200,000-subscriber influencer...

42
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,240
Slide five! Slide five!

43
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,079
Read everything and summarize the previous campaign issues.

44
00:03:27,079 --> 00:03:28,720
Separate the client contact list

45
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,200
from the KOL list,

46
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,280
and prioritize the most urgent tasks.

47
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,800
I want it on my desk

48
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:34,800
before noon.

49
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,560
Understood.

50
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,480
Save that shocked expression

51
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,760
for when you actually mess up.

52
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:13,680
Right now,

53
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:16,279
you'd better start reading faster.

54
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,880
I don't like working with slow people.

55
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:24,880
Understood.

56
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:56,960
If it were me,

57
00:04:57,159 --> 00:04:58,840
I'd sort these documents

58
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,920
by how much damage each campaign caused,

59
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,160
not by these cute

60
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,600
pastel colors.

61
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:08,920
Put any project that could cost the company

62
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,680
hundreds of millions in penalties

63
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,920
right on top.

64
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,520
And the projects with fewer client complaints

65
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:15,680
go at the bottom.

66
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:19,080
Learn to rank your crises,

67
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,880
and you'll know which file to take

68
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,160
to Ms. Nannalin first.

69
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,320
That's true.

70
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:31,240
Sort them by severity.

71
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,560
P'Nida!

72
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,280
Thank you!

73
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,880
Come to think of it,

74
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:49,159
everyone here has such clearly defined roles.

75
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,880
And they're all incredibly good at their jobs.

76
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,040
Take P'Nida, for example.

77
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,360
She may seem cold and stuck-up,

78
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:58,440
but her advice about organizing files

79
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,800
really saved my life.

80
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,120
And P'Pim...

81
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,920
She's so sweet!

82
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,080
She's practically the AE team's guardian angel.

83
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:09,880
She's always ready to rescue me from my mountain of work.

84
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,120
And then...

85
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:14,240
What about P'Nui?

86
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:16,040
The one who's always snacking?

87
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:19,520
Oh, she's a real character.

88
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:24,840
She's the department's fake-news station
and champion work-shirker.

89
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:48,240
Excuse me.

90
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,560
Where are the desks for the...

91
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:59,080
exclusive content creator team?

92
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:01,320
It's my first day here. I'm Mueanfan.

93
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,120
Thank you!

94
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:23,640
Pim!

95
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,640
This year's new hires

96
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,360
couldn't be more different.

97
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,720
They're both making quite an entrance.

98
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:30,440
How so?

99
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:33,840
One showed up with her portfolio, ready to fight for her life.

100
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:36,440
She looks like a soap-opera heroine,

101
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:37,760
all set to be bossed around.

102
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:39,760
And the other one

103
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,920
is a pampered little princess.

104
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:44,840
She looks like an intern with connections.

105
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:46,840
Keep your voice down.

106
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:50,159
It's barely morning and you're already gossiping?

107
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:52,280
If anyone hears you,

108
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:53,560
we'll all be in trouble.

109
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,120
I don't care!

110
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,760
How's it going, Alice?

111
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:17,880
Oh, God...

112
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,080
I'm almost there.

113
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:21,880
Almost ready to melt into fertilizer right here.

114
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,600
There's so much work, P'Pim!

115
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,440
And it's all due by noon.

116
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:30,280
Oh, come here. I'll help you.

117
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:33,720
I'll list the campaigns and client names for you,

118
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:36,320
so you won't waste time digging through those thick files.

119
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:39,559
And I'll also...

120
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:42,120
check each project's schedule for you.

121
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:45,000
I'll see which ones need rates within half an hour,

122
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,040
And which tasks would be disastrous if delayed.

123
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,920
My soul will leave my body!

124
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,560
That way, we'll finish everything before noon.

125
00:08:58,800 --> 00:08:59,600
Nui!

126
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:03,000
You snuck off to the convenience store again, didn't you?

127
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:06,200
Have you finished the design for page four?

128
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:07,920
Oh, my goodness!

129
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:10,520
What a terrible accusation, Pim!

130
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,160
I wasn't slacking off.

131
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,440
I was gathering supplies

132
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,080
to recharge poor Alice!

133
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:17,920
Look at her.

134
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:21,000
She's working herself half to death.

135
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,680
Oh! Thank you, P'Nui.

136
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:31,800
But you know what?

137
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,400
Let me tell you something.

138
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:35,800
I think you've got some kind of magnetic energy,

139
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:37,920
or maybe you're destined for something.

140
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,760
On your very first day,

141
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:43,080
you somehow attracted Ms. Nannalin's attention.

142
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,320
She summoned you to her office,

143
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,160
and gave you the toughest assignments

144
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:49,160
first thing in the morning!

145
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:50,560
Sigh...

146
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,800
That's enough, Nui.

147
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,720
What magnetic energy?

148
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,040
The energy she's dealing with right now

149
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,400
is called

150
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,160
work

151
00:09:58,160 --> 00:09:58,960
over

152
00:09:58,960 --> 00:09:59,840
load!

153
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:03,040
Why else would she be working herself into a frenzy?

154
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,280
You've got a point.

155
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,120
She's really in trouble.

156
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:09,080
Seriously.

157
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,840
There's definitely energy here.

158
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:14,400
A whole avalanche of work on my desk!

159
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:17,520
And I've only got one hour left.

160
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,040
I don't know if I'll finish in time.

161
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,080
Of course you will.

162
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,600
You're in good hands.

163
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,800
We'll both help you sort out the schedule.

164
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,080
Let's finish our own work first.

165
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:30,040
Before we help Alice, let's help ourselves first.

166
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,960
The beauty campaign isn't finished yet.

167
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,240
We'd better hurry.

168
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:35,600
Otherwise, when Ms. Narin arrives,

169
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:38,320
she'll come straight for us.

170
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,120
We'll be dead!

171
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,360
Oh, that's right!

172
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:46,080
I completely forgot!

173
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,880
Well, then...

174
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,600
We'd better

175
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:52,000
finish our own work first.

176
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,720
Hang in there, Alice!

177
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:17,520
Alice!

178
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:20,920
I really need your help.

179
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,680
Um, what's wrong?

180
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:25,400
Well...

181
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:28,280
I made a draft content file

182
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:30,120
to send to the graphics team,

183
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:32,120
but somehow it's disappeared.

184
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,520
I checked the cloud,

185
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,320
and I can't find it anywhere.

186
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:39,720
Can you help me recover or find it?

187
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,160
It's just that...

188
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,880
I've still got a ton of work

189
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:51,280
for Ms. Nannalin,

190
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:52,920
and it's all due before noon.

191
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,520
Please!

192
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:57,560
Alice, please help me.

193
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:00,000
It's my first day, and...

194
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,640
I'm terrible with computers.

195
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,600
I don't know who else to ask.

196
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:08,680
If I can't submit the draft on time,

197
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,480
I'm definitely going to get scolded.

198
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,200
Please help me.

199
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,920
Okay, okay. I'll

200
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,560
check the trash folder for you.

201
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:33,880
Okay.

202
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:34,760
Thanks, Alice!

203
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,680
Oh, Alice!

204
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,480
I wasn't slacking off, sweetheart.

205
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,160
I was just...

206
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,400
low on sugar.

207
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:23,160
My blood sugar dropped.

208
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:25,080
You know, a sudden sugar crash?

209
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:26,880
And it's break time anyway.

210
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:27,880
I'm just taking a break

211
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:30,440
to clear my mind and recharge my creativity.

212
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:33,720
We're creating world-class art here!

213
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,240
Believe me!

214
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:39,440
I haven't even said a word yet!

215
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:42,920
Nui!

216
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,120
Sneaking off to slack again, I see.

217
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:48,600
You're always the first to disappear.

218
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,480
Seriously, tell me something.

219
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,400
Do you have some kind of slacker radar

220
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:55,920
implanted in your eyeballs?

221
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,360
You're always catching me!

222
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,400
Am I really that obvious?

223
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:03,440
You've been obvious from the start.

224
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,440
Your face

225
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:08,320
has 'slacker' written all over it.

226
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:09,960
Anyone who can't see that

227
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,120
must be blind.

228
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,360
Where? Can I wipe it off?

229
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:17,200
Finish eating and go fix that draft. Now!

230
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,200
But I'm hungry!

231
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:27,960
Hello, Ms. Nannalin.

232
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,040
You're out of iced tea?

233
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,320
Of course. I'll bring it right away.

234
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:44,120
See you, P'Pim, P'Nui!

235
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:46,760
Go on!

236
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:51,760
Is it good?

237
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,160
Delicious. Want some?

238
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,680
So rich!

239
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,800
But the person who stresses me out the most

240
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,080
is Ms. Nannalin.

241
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:10,720
Here you go.

242
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,080
The structure is acceptable.

243
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:50,000
You've identified the campaign's main problems well,

244
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,320
but it's not sharp enough.

245
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:57,800
You have plenty of data,

246
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,920
but lack strategic analysis.

247
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,120
You can identify problems,

248
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,720
but not practical solutions.

249
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,160
Take it back and revise it.

250
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,840
Divide your recommendations into three phases:

251
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:20,920
most urgent,

252
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:22,560
medium priority,

253
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:24,800
and contingency plan.

254
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,880
I'll revise it as quickly as possible.

255
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:39,520
If you want to secure your place here,

256
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:43,760
you need to understand that in the real working world,

257
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:47,280
effort alone is never enough.

258
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:50,280
Because everyone is trying hard.

259
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:56,640
I don't need to see your sweat.

260
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,720
I need quality results.

261
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:05,720
Understood.

262
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:08,480
I'll submit a much sharper draft

263
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:11,520
before noon, Ms. Nannalin.

264
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:24,359
Wow, this doesn't sound like a first day at work.

265
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:26,839
You're like a little lamb

266
00:17:27,599 --> 00:17:29,760
thrown into a tiger's cage.

267
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,440
But what's amazing

268
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:35,920
is that the tiger's cage smells of hot tea!

269
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:44,520
She's so intimidating I almost forgot how to breathe.

270
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:47,040
She's the kind of boss who's...

271
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:49,920
Too beautiful.

272
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:51,320
I mean,

273
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,400
her beauty doesn't match how ruthless she is.

274
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,880
She's as strict as a drill sergeant.

275
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,200
Beautiful?

276
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:01,320
How beautiful?

277
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,960
I thought she was an evil witch.

278
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:05,480
How come

279
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:08,120
she's suddenly too beautiful as well,

280
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:08,720
Ms. Assistant?

281
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:09,720
Hmph!

282
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,160
I'm talking about her suits!

283
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:15,080
Her suits are perfectly tailored every day.

284
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:16,920
Beautiful.

285
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,360
Way too beautiful.

286
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:27,680
Ugh.

287
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:29,480
This sucks.

288
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,840
If I didn't have another event to attend,

289
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,160
I'd keep you here all night

290
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:35,480
so you could blow off some steam.

291
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,880
Go take care of work first.

292
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:39,480
We can meet anytime.

293
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:41,840
And you, too.

294
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:45,080
Don't work yourself to death without resting.

295
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:48,520
You look like a zombie after just one day.

296
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:52,200
After a month, your soul might leave your body!

297
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:55,640
I'll get used to it.

298
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:59,240
It's only my first day of getting beaten down.

299
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:03,440
My body will build up immunity eventually.

300
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,080
Whatever helps you sleep at night.

301
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:09,560
But let me warn you:

302
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:12,000
Work hard all you want,

303
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,880
but don't tie yourself

304
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,200
or your heart

305
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,360
to that beautiful boss.

306
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,480
I'm warning you for your own good.

307
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:24,840
Hey, hey!

308
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,520
Hello, Ms. Nannalin.

309
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,040
Please find Ms. Ratee's background and personal information.

310
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,440
I want an in-depth profile,

311
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,760
including her personal lifestyle,

312
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,200
her favorite luxury brands,

313
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:51,680
and most importantly,

314
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:54,880
find some interesting talking points

315
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,640
I can use to open a conversation

316
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,240
and break the ice with her.

317
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:00,600
Um, of course.

318
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:02,640
How urgently do you need it,

319
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:03,880
Ms. Nannalin?

320
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:05,680
Before I have to ask for it.

321
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:06,120
What?

322
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,040
Why?

323
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:13,360
You're in trouble now.

324
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:20,880
An assignment that requires psychic powers?

325
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:26,200
Someone else would've thrown their resignation in her face.

326
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:27,880
Hey!

327
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:29,680
It's really fate!

328
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:32,080
Good luck, my friend!

329
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,880
I'm rooting for you!

330
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:37,080
I've got to find information for Ms. Narin first.

331
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:38,560
Okay, see you!

332
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,480
Yeah, yeah!

333
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,000
Thank you, thank you!

334
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,360
No sleep for you tonight.

335
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:47,800
Hey!

336
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:48,880
Wait!

337
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,480
At least pay your bill first!

338
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:58,880
Excuse me.

339
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:17,480
Are you going to stand there all day?

340
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:20,560
Um...

341
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,000
I'm sorry.

342
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:29,120
These are

343
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:32,880
the documents I prepared on Ms. Ratee.

344
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:34,560
They cover her background,

345
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,480
lifestyle, favorite brands,

346
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:38,040
and favorite places.

347
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:43,080
I've also included some conversation starters.

348
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:52,520
Ms. Ratee dislikes aggressive salespeople.

349
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:54,880
Oh.

350
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:56,320
Okay.

351
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:59,080
She dislikes scripted compliments.

352
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:00,760
Understood.

353
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:03,920
And she dislikes people who think quiet luxury

354
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,480
just means wearing beige.

355
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:06,920
Understood.

356
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:08,480
You're coming with me tomorrow.

357
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:10,240
Pardon?

358
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:15,320
Um...

359
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:16,360
You mean...

360
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,320
I'm going with you, Ms. Nannalin?

361
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:19,120
Yes.

362
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:21,640
To meet Ms. Ratee together?

363
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:26,400
Did I say something else?

364
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:29,400
No.

365
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,080
You don't need to talk much.

366
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:36,480
Tomorrow, your job is to

367
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:36,720
watch,

368
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:37,360
listen,

369
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:38,800
and remember.

370
00:22:41,280 --> 00:22:43,120
Answer only if I ask you something.

371
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:46,840
If I don't ask, don't speak.

372
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:47,960
Okay.

373
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:53,640
Dress nicely tomorrow.

374
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:55,960
Huh?

375
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:57,640
Elegantly but professionally.

376
00:22:58,320 --> 00:23:00,000
Not like you're going to a party.

377
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:02,840
And don't be so conservative

378
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,000
that you look like you're taking a civil service exam.

379
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:06,480
Ah.

380
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:07,840
Understood.

381
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:10,160
Elegant and professional.

382
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:11,040
Not a party outfit,

383
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:13,880
and not too formal either.

384
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:31,960
Your heart is beating so fast.

385
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:36,760
Oh.

386
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:41,080
I'm excited about tomorrow's meeting.

387
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:43,240
Just like that night.

388
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,880
Ms. Nannalin...

389
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:50,560
You remember?

390
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,640
Did you really think I'd forget

391
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:56,760
someone who saved my dress from disaster

392
00:23:58,080 --> 00:23:59,080
and also

393
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:00,840
ruined my plans

394
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:02,320
so easily?

395
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:09,080
Um, I thought...

396
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,680
Ms. Nannalin...

397
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,920
Dress nicely tomorrow.

398
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:27,840
And pay attention to

399
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:29,080
what I'm going to teach you.

400
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:33,520
Yes.

401
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,080
You may go home now.

402
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:41,400
See you tomorrow at eight sharp.

403
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:44,840
Yes.

404
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,600
She actually remembers?

405
00:25:06,600 --> 00:25:07,560
It's a business meeting.

406
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,880
Just a business meeting.

407
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,160
Don't think about the kiss.

408
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:11,920
Absolutely don't think about the kiss.

409
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:14,360
Oh, God!

410
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:16,720
I've already thought about it!

411
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:22,400
Do you know the biggest twist in the series? Yeah?

412
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:22,880
The male lead...

413
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:25,080
Guess who he kisses in the cave instead of me?

414
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,680
The second male lead! Oh, God!

415
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:29,280
I was shocked! Why didn't he kiss me?

416
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:30,760
What show were you even watching?

417
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:32,600
I want to be in it so badly!

418
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:34,080
People really get obsessed, huh?

419
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,400
Oh, my goodness!

420
00:25:36,840 --> 00:25:39,600
Alice is dressed like a proper young manager today!

421
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:41,760
What do you think? Does it work?

422
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:43,880
Very polished!

423
00:25:44,280 --> 00:25:45,520
Do you have a date,

424
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:47,360
or is it a special occasion?

425
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:47,800
What?

426
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:50,320
Alice, of all people,

427
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:51,480
is dressed so neatly,

428
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:53,960
from her collar down to her trousers.

429
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:55,760
With an outfit like this,

430
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:59,440
I'm a hundred percent sure she's meeting a client

431
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,280
with Ms. Nannalin.

432
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:02,960
You know too much!

433
00:26:05,600 --> 00:26:06,400
You there.

434
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:08,680
Yes?

435
00:26:08,720 --> 00:26:10,960
If you're meeting a client with Ms. Nannalin today,

436
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:12,440
make sure

437
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:14,800
you're not wearing strong perfume,

438
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:17,360
especially anything sickly sweet

439
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,360
or a trendy, overpowering fragrance.

440
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:22,280
Our client is a VIP

441
00:26:22,760 --> 00:26:24,600
and very sensitive to scents.

442
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:27,480
Of course, of course.

443
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:29,480
I'm not wearing any perfume today.

444
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:30,480
Thank you for warning me.

445
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:41,040
Alice.

446
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:43,480
Um...

447
00:26:45,200 --> 00:26:47,240
I need another favor.

448
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:51,080
I was trying to upload

449
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:53,920
my idea summary to the shared drive, but...

450
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:56,600
somehow

451
00:26:56,600 --> 00:27:00,280
it ended up in the account folder.

452
00:27:00,280 --> 00:27:01,240
I don't know how to move it.

453
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:04,040
I tried, but I couldn't do it.

454
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:06,680
Could you help me?

455
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:09,160
Hmm.

456
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:13,720
Okay. I'll move it for you.

457
00:27:22,840 --> 00:27:26,440
There. I've moved it to the creative content folder.

458
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:28,600
That was so fast!

459
00:27:28,600 --> 00:27:29,840
Thanks, Alice!

460
00:27:29,840 --> 00:27:32,280
You're the kindest and sweetest person!

461
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:32,880
Thank you!

462
00:27:47,880 --> 00:27:50,160
Here's the detailed profile summary

463
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:53,720
and the suggested conversation starters for Ms. Ratee.

464
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:14,440
Good summary.

465
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:19,920
You've accurately identified her sophisticated tastes,

466
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:22,640
her appreciation for intricate design,

467
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:26,600
and the way she socializes.

468
00:28:27,720 --> 00:28:29,440
Especially your suggestions

469
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:32,560
for icebreakers.

470
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:36,680
Thank you.

471
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:39,680
Actually, after reviewing her background

472
00:28:39,680 --> 00:28:41,440
and lifestyle,

473
00:28:41,440 --> 00:28:43,840
I think it's more than personal preferences.

474
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:45,440
Ms. Ratee

475
00:28:45,440 --> 00:28:46,960
carefully decides

476
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:49,640
how she wants people to see her,

477
00:28:49,720 --> 00:28:53,040
and who gets to see which side of her.

478
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:00,760
You're starting to understand.

479
00:29:10,960 --> 00:29:12,800
Tea.

480
00:29:16,160 --> 00:29:17,080
Of course.

481
00:29:17,080 --> 00:29:19,480
I'll bring you hot tea at the perfect temperature

482
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:20,680
and have it on your desk

483
00:29:20,680 --> 00:29:22,080
within three minutes.

484
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:32,080
Water at just the right temperature,

485
00:29:32,080 --> 00:29:33,400
steeped perfectly, not too weak or bitter, sweet or cold.

486
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:34,920
Not too weak or bitter,

487
00:29:34,920 --> 00:29:36,800
not sweet or cold.

488
00:29:47,440 --> 00:29:49,160
Are you brewing tea,

489
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:51,240
or reciting some kind of spirit-summoning ritual?

490
00:29:52,080 --> 00:29:53,800
I'm making tea for Ms. Nannalin.

491
00:29:54,360 --> 00:29:55,760
Then it's not tea-making.

492
00:29:56,320 --> 00:29:57,600
It's preparing a sacred offering!

493
00:29:58,280 --> 00:30:00,320
Oh, P'Nui!

494
00:30:01,040 --> 00:30:01,600
Sigh...

495
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:03,400
I'd better stop bothering you.

496
00:30:03,400 --> 00:30:06,120
Our rookie is about to enter the battlefield. Respect!

497
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:08,720
I'm showing respect!

498
00:30:13,440 --> 00:30:15,040
Great color, great aroma.

499
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:21,960
Oh!

500
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:29,960
Congratulations!

501
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:33,480
You've passed the first trial of the Witch of Lune!

502
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:37,200
I haven't even given it to Ms. Nannalin yet.

503
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:38,320
Then you haven't passed yet.

504
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:40,960
You've only made it through the preliminaries.

505
00:30:50,360 --> 00:30:52,400
Ms. Ratee is here. What?

506
00:30:53,280 --> 00:30:54,480
We have to go meet her.

507
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:56,320
Right now?

508
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:58,680
We can wait until tomorrow,

509
00:30:58,680 --> 00:30:59,520
if you prefer.

510
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:07,400
And your tea was going so well today.

511
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:12,560
Please take care of this, P'Nui.

512
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:17,720
Oh, dear.

513
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:20,560
A prince born at the wrong time.

514
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:26,680
Breathe.

515
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:28,520
Yes?

516
00:31:29,760 --> 00:31:36,400
Today you watch, listen, and remember. Don't speak unless I ask.

517
00:31:38,040 --> 00:31:38,880
Understood.

518
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:49,960
Hello.

519
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:53,360
I'm sorry I arrived early.

520
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:54,680
Not at all.

521
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:57,560
It's lovely to see you. Please have a seat.

522
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:08,200
You look wonderful today, Ms. Ratee.

523
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:11,680
Especially that Hermès scarf.

524
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:15,880
The delicate print and lightweight fabric

525
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:18,960
remind me of an afternoon in Kashmir.

526
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:22,520
You have a keen eye, Ms. Nan.

527
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:28,000
I chose this scarf because it reminded me of Kashmir, too.

528
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:32,400
I never overlook beautiful things

529
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:35,400
that have stories hidden in them.

530
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:44,000
I'm launching a new cosmetics line of my own.

531
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,120
And I'd love for Lune Agency

532
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:49,640
to manage it and develop a strategy for the brand.

533
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:52,040
That includes new product launches,

534
00:32:52,560 --> 00:32:55,480
KOL coordination and events,

535
00:32:55,480 --> 00:32:58,240
and especially media PR.

536
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:02,320
That sounds like a fascinating project, Ms. Ratee.

537
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:06,120
And when it comes to brand ambassadors,

538
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:08,440
do you have anyone in mind?

539
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:13,320
I'm considering Namhom and Preem.

540
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:17,320
One is a hugely popular actress,

541
00:33:17,320 --> 00:33:18,560
and the other

542
00:33:18,560 --> 00:33:20,400
is a top beauty blogger.

543
00:33:21,280 --> 00:33:23,920
They both have strong fan bases,

544
00:33:23,920 --> 00:33:26,080
which would be great for a new brand.

545
00:33:28,200 --> 00:33:31,000
Those are interesting choices.

546
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:34,160
So your cosmetics brand

547
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:36,880
isn't just selling youthful beauty.

548
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:40,000
It's selling confidence

549
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:44,320
and the power of women who choose to care
for themselves with taste,

550
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:47,400
without seeking anyone else's approval.

551
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:50,040
Exactly.

552
00:33:50,040 --> 00:33:53,080
This brand is a matter of pride for me.

553
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:57,320
If I can make it successful,

554
00:33:58,080 --> 00:33:59,360
I hope

555
00:33:59,360 --> 00:34:02,160
someone as important as Ms. Rinrada

556
00:34:02,160 --> 00:34:03,760
will see what I'm capable of.

557
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:09,159
I'm counting on you.

558
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:12,600
Absolutely.

559
00:34:16,199 --> 00:34:17,480
Ms. Nannalin.

560
00:34:19,199 --> 00:34:20,639
You're incredible.

561
00:34:22,239 --> 00:34:23,320
Did you only just realize that?

562
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:28,000
I've always known you were good.

563
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:31,080
But today I saw for myself

564
00:34:31,080 --> 00:34:33,800
just how well you can read people.

565
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:35,400
The scarf,

566
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:37,000
Ms. Ratee,

567
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:43,800
and the way you didn't have to sell
anything to make her feel understood.

568
00:34:50,679 --> 00:34:51,560
Sorry.

569
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:57,040
What you witnessed today wasn't a trick for flattering clients.

570
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:01,760
It was listening beyond the words they say.

571
00:35:05,120 --> 00:35:06,120
Ms. Ratee

572
00:35:06,600 --> 00:35:09,560
doesn't just need us to sell lipstick.

573
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:12,600
She needs this brand

574
00:35:12,600 --> 00:35:15,360
to prove something about who she is.

575
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:19,600
You mean to Ms. Rinrada?

576
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:25,520
Sorry.

577
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:27,560
I shouldn't have...

578
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:30,840
No, this time you're right.

579
00:35:32,600 --> 00:35:34,600
But even when you're right,

580
00:35:34,600 --> 00:35:36,280
you need to know when to keep it to yourself.

581
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:39,200
Not every truth

582
00:35:39,200 --> 00:35:41,600
needs to be spoken immediately.

583
00:35:43,760 --> 00:35:44,720
I understand.

584
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:09,600
Your lipstick...

585
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:15,200
It's a pretty shade.

586
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:20,360
It suits you.

587
00:36:33,160 --> 00:36:35,200
Is that still part of the lesson?

588
00:36:59,080 --> 00:37:00,760
Well, well, Ms. Assistant!

589
00:37:02,080 --> 00:37:05,040
You look awfully pleased with yourself.

590
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:11,480
Is it the heat outside, or is there another
reason your cheeks are red?

591
00:37:11,720 --> 00:37:12,520
Ah!

592
00:37:13,560 --> 00:37:15,760
You scared me, P'Nui!

593
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:21,400
I was only asking whether the client meeting went well.

594
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:24,600
Oh... yes, it did.

595
00:37:25,200 --> 00:37:26,800
Ms. Natty was really nice.

596
00:37:27,480 --> 00:37:28,960
Your voice is all squeaky.

597
00:37:29,120 --> 00:37:30,480
And that answer was suspiciously short.

598
00:37:30,800 --> 00:37:31,960
You're hiding something!

599
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:35,320
Oh, come on!

600
00:37:35,640 --> 00:37:37,840
I need to upload these files to my computer.

601
00:37:43,280 --> 00:37:44,080
Hmm.

602
00:37:44,320 --> 00:37:46,320
That settles it. Something's going on.

603
00:37:46,640 --> 00:37:47,040
Hmph.

604
00:37:47,040 --> 00:37:49,000
Aren't you overthinking things, Nui?

605
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:52,720
Alice might just have stayed up all night working.

606
00:37:52,720 --> 00:37:54,280
That could explain why she looks dazed and flushed.

607
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:55,960
How can you be so sure?

608
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:57,400
Do you have evidence?

609
00:37:58,000 --> 00:37:59,360
There goes your rumor mill again.

610
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:01,840
The evidence is written all over Alice's face.

611
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:03,040
Usually,

612
00:38:03,040 --> 00:38:05,000
when Ms. Nannalin gives her a hard time,

613
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:08,240
she turns pale as a ghost.

614
00:38:08,240 --> 00:38:09,120
But look at her now!

615
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:12,920
Rosy cheeks and dreamy eyes!

616
00:38:13,200 --> 00:38:16,920
She's acting exactly like someone who's fallen in love!

617
00:38:18,040 --> 00:38:20,320
Pim, let me warn you.

618
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:23,960
Don't listen too much to Nui's fake-news channel.

619
00:38:23,960 --> 00:38:25,360
It'll rot your brain.

620
00:38:26,040 --> 00:38:27,720
Are you prejudiced against me?

621
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:32,080
I've actually studied advanced office psychology!

622
00:38:32,080 --> 00:38:34,600
I may not look like it, but I read books!

623
00:38:34,600 --> 00:38:36,160
Alice's behavior

624
00:38:36,160 --> 00:38:37,800
is exactly what you see when someone

625
00:38:37,800 --> 00:38:40,360
tries to act normal,

626
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:42,840
but just ends up looking even less normal.

627
00:38:44,720 --> 00:38:47,200
And here's the overview of our campaign.

628
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:52,000
Our mood and tone will focus on fun, energy, and vibrancy.

629
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:54,800
We'll bring youthful spirit to the world,

630
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:56,840
with an emphasis on freshness,

631
00:38:56,840 --> 00:38:58,760
a full hundred percent.

632
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:00,160
Thank you.

633
00:39:04,360 --> 00:39:05,160
Ms. Nui,

634
00:39:08,240 --> 00:39:11,600
if a woman older than your main target demographic

635
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:13,320
saw this campaign,

636
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:15,760
do you think she'd be interested

637
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:19,160
in buying this cosmetics brand?

638
00:39:20,480 --> 00:39:24,640
But our primary target audience is

639
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:26,880
university students to early-career women, Ms. Narin.

640
00:39:28,120 --> 00:39:30,160
Ms. Ratee's idea of freshness

641
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:32,200
doesn't necessarily mean being young

642
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:34,000
or being a teenager.

643
00:39:34,720 --> 00:39:36,800
A fresh start and a sense of renewal

644
00:39:36,800 --> 00:39:43,640
can belong to women of any age. A good
cosmetics brand shouldn't build walls

645
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:46,520
or exclude any group of women

646
00:39:47,400 --> 00:39:50,320
just because they aren't the market's ideal age.

647
00:39:53,440 --> 00:39:59,160
Ms. Ratee wants luxury, confidence, and
results that reflect her identity.

648
00:40:00,680 --> 00:40:03,360
Revise this project's mood and tone.

649
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:05,880
Add an element of accessible luxury,

650
00:40:06,760 --> 00:40:10,040
and bring out a mature, sophisticated freshness.

651
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:13,040
Absolutely, Ms. Nannalin.

652
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:15,200
That's a brilliant idea.

653
00:40:15,200 --> 00:40:18,160
My team and I will rework everything

654
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:20,640
and make the concept as sharp as possible.

655
00:40:21,240 --> 00:40:22,040
Thank you.

656
00:40:23,520 --> 00:40:25,600
Please move quickly.

657
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:29,200
This project is urgent and very important to our company.

658
00:40:30,120 --> 00:40:30,600
Of course.

659
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:33,520
We'll get it done as soon as possible.

660
00:40:40,400 --> 00:40:42,920
Is something urgent, Ms. Rinrada?

661
00:40:45,240 --> 00:40:48,800
I heard the new cosmetics campaign

662
00:40:49,400 --> 00:40:51,720
you just had a meeting about

663
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:53,920
belongs to Ms. Ratee. Is that right?

664
00:40:55,440 --> 00:40:56,240
Yes.

665
00:41:00,720 --> 00:41:01,880
That's rather strange.

666
00:41:03,560 --> 00:41:06,200
Someone as meticulous and ambitious as Ratee...

667
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:09,760
Why would she come to an agency like ours?

668
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:21,760
Do you have insider information or concerns
about this project, Ms. Rinrada?

669
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:26,240
Nothing in particular.

670
00:41:26,600 --> 00:41:29,280
I just want you to examine the project carefully.

671
00:41:30,200 --> 00:41:33,200
I'm worried she might have a hidden agenda

672
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:35,200
behind all that advertising money.

673
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:40,840
For now, the contract says Lune

674
00:41:40,840 --> 00:41:43,480
will handle only the overall brand strategy.

675
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:46,800
As for the finer details and other obligations,

676
00:41:46,800 --> 00:41:49,280
those are still under careful review.

677
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,560
You can rest assured, Ms. Rinrada.

678
00:41:53,120 --> 00:41:54,560
Well, that's a relief.

679
00:41:58,000 --> 00:41:58,760
Oh, and...

680
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:02,560
that new assistant of yours,

681
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:07,120
how is she doing after her first couple of
days? Is she keeping up?

682
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:11,400
Not with everything yet.

683
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:14,040
She's still a little flustered sometimes,

684
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:18,320
but overall she's improving steadily.

685
00:42:20,200 --> 00:42:21,160
Auntie!

686
00:42:22,160 --> 00:42:22,960
Hello!

687
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:28,920
Um, sorry.

688
00:42:29,800 --> 00:42:31,560
Hello, Ms. Rinrada.

689
00:42:36,160 --> 00:42:39,760
How's work in this department? Any problems?

690
00:42:40,640 --> 00:42:41,920
Hmm...

691
00:42:41,920 --> 00:42:42,880
It's fun!

692
00:42:42,880 --> 00:42:46,720
Everyone on the team is kind and always helps me.

693
00:42:49,040 --> 00:42:50,000
That's good.

694
00:42:50,640 --> 00:42:52,880
Work hard here.

695
00:42:53,200 --> 00:42:55,880
Learn as much as you can from your seniors.

696
00:42:57,120 --> 00:42:59,920
Don't waste your time wandering around, or you'll learn nothing.

697
00:43:01,600 --> 00:43:02,440
Yes.

698
00:43:03,040 --> 00:43:05,880
I'll get back to work, then.

699
00:43:05,880 --> 00:43:07,800
Work mode!

700
00:43:36,760 --> 00:43:41,360
Namhom is pretty, but her eyes look a bit empty.

701
00:43:44,080 --> 00:43:45,760
Do you have too much free time, Alice?

702
00:43:45,760 --> 00:43:46,640
You may be kind, Alice,

703
00:43:46,640 --> 00:43:48,800
but you're not very smart, are you?

704
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:49,560
Get in.

705
00:43:50,280 --> 00:43:51,680
Or do I have to come down and pick you up?

706
00:43:52,120 --> 00:43:54,520
How can anyone drink this much tea every day?

707
00:43:54,960 --> 00:43:57,120
It stops me from killing people in meetings.

708
00:43:57,640 --> 00:43:59,800
Then you should drink plenty of it!

709
00:44:00,320 --> 00:44:02,120
You're already blushing from seeing my underwear.

710
00:44:02,600 --> 00:44:04,000
If you saw me wearing it,

711
00:44:04,000 --> 00:44:06,640
wouldn't you have a heart attack, Ms. Alice?
